e shake-flask method. The complexes were dissolved in the aqueous phase saturated with n-octanol, and an equal volume of the organic phase saturated with water was added and mixed uniformly. The mixture was shaken overnight at 37 °C and 800 rpm, then centrifuged at 8000 rpm for 8 min. The absorbance of the complexes in the organic and aqueous phases was detected using a UV–vis spectrophotometer, and the log Po/w value was calculated."},{"abbreviation_in_the_article":"Ir-NH2","value":1.75,"value_relation":"=","type_authors":"logP","method":"shake-flask","aqueous_phase":"0.9% NaCl","doi":"10.1021/acs.jmedchem.4c00404","year":2024,"counterion":"F[P-](F)(F)(F)(F)F","record_id":"MLDB-003738","detection":"UV-Vis","method_description":"According to the reported procedure, (53) the lipophilicity (Log Po/w) of Ir-UA and Ir-NH2 was measured by the flask-shaking method."},{"abbreviation_in_the_article":"Ir-NH2","value":0.32,"value_relation":"=","type_authors":"logP","method":"shake-flask","aqueous_phase":"PBS","doi":"10.1016/j.ica.2025.122601","year":2025,"counterion":"F[P-](F)(F)(F)(F)F","record_id":"MLDB-003938","detection":"UV-Vis","method_description":"The lipophilicity was determined using the shake flask method. bpy-NPX, Ir-NH2, and Ir-NPX were dissolved in PBS buffer at equal concentrations of 20 μM and pre-saturated with n-octanol. An equal volume of n-octanol solution saturated with PBS buffer was added to each compound. The mixture was shaken in the dark for 8 h at room temperature. The two phases were separated by centrifugation, and the absorbance of the compounds in the organic phase and the aqueous phase was measured using UV-vis spectroscopy. The log Po/w is defined as the logarithmic ratio of the concentration of the sample in the organic phase to the aqueous phase."},{"abbreviation_in_the_article":"Ir-NH2","value":1.03,"value_relation":"=","type_authors":"logP","method":"shake-flask","aqueous_phase":"0.9% NaCl","doi":"10.1002/anie.202203843","year":2022,"counterion":"F[P-](F)(F)(F)(F)F","record_id":"MLDB-004175","detection":"UV-Vis","method_description":"The lipophilicity of Ir-NH2 and Ir-Rhein was determined by measuring the value of log Po/w, which was referred to as the octanol-water partition coefficients, following a reported procedure.6"}]}